  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Find the derivative of each function, and by solving $y'>0$, find the values of $x$ for which the function is increasing.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=x^2-4x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=2x-4$; increasing for $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=2x-4\\\\2x-4&>0\\\\2x&>4\\\\x&>2\\end{align*}$$\nThe function is increasing for $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=7-6x-x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=-6-2x$; increasing for $x<-3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=-6-2x\\\\-6-2x&>0\\\\-2x&>6\\\\x&<-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe function is increasing for $x<-3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=2x^3-6x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=6x^2-6$; increasing for $x<-1$ or $x>1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=6x^2-6\\\\6x^2-6&>0\\\\6(x-1)(x+1)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe derivative is an upward-opening quadratic with zeros $-1$ and $1$, so it is positive outside these zeros.\n\nThe function is increasing for $x<-1$ or $x>1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q15-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=x^3-3x^2+7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y'=3x^2-6x$; increasing for $x<0$ or $x>2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=3x^2-6x\\\\3x^2-6x&>0\\\\3x(x-2)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe derivative is an upward-opening quadratic with zeros $0$ and $2$, so it is positive outside these zeros.\n\nThe function is increasing for $x<0$ or $x>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
